---
layout: base.njk
title: Swiss pharmaceutical scientist
description: "Personal website of Adriano Rutz — Swiss pharmaceutical scientist specialising in metabolomics, mass spectrometry, and natural products research."
permalink: /index.html
---
<article class="home" vocab="https://schema.org/" typeof="ProfilePage" resource="{{ site.url }}/">

  <header class="hero" property="mainEntity" typeof="Person" about="wd:Q97455964" resource="{{ site.url }}/#me">
    {# srcset: the portrait is the LCP element on this page, so it should not be
       a compromise size for every display. width/height reserve the box; the
       sizes attribute lets the browser pick before layout. #}
    <picture class="hero__avatar">
      <source type="image/avif"
        srcset="/images/profile/avatar-150.avif 150w,
                /images/profile/avatar-260.avif 260w,
                /images/profile/avatar-520.avif 520w"
        sizes="(max-width: 36rem) 5.5rem, (max-width: 48rem) 6.5rem, 9rem" />
      <img src="/images/profile/avatar-260.webp"
        srcset="/images/profile/avatar-150.webp 150w,
                /images/profile/avatar-260.webp 260w,
                /images/profile/avatar-520.webp 520w"
        sizes="(max-width: 36rem) 5.5rem, (max-width: 48rem) 6.5rem, 9rem"
        width="150" height="150"
        alt="" property="image" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" />
    </picture>
     {# One top-level heading: the name, with the role folded in as a
        visually-subdued span. WAVE flags a paragraph styled like a byline as a
        "possible heading"; co-locating the role inside the h1 removes that
        heading-like paragraph entirely while keeping the page's single
        top-level heading. The portrait's alt is empty: the name is right
        beside it in this heading, so repeating it there is the redundancy
        WAVE flags. #}
     <h1 class="hero__name p-name"><span property="name">Adriano Rutz</span><span class="hero__role" property="jobTitle">, Swiss pharmaceutical scientist</span></h1>
     <div class="hero__text">
       <p class="hero__lede" property="description">
        Metabolomics, mass spectrometry, open science, and natural products — currently at the
        <span property="affiliation" typeof="Organization" about="wd:Q11942"><span property="name">Institute for Molecular Systems Biology at ETH Zurich</span></span>.
      </p>
      {# Contact details, not publication profiles. Someone landing here wants to
         reach you; the scholarly identifiers belong with the articles, which is
         where they are. #}
      <ul class="identifiers" aria-label="Contact">
        <li><a href="mailto:{{ site.contact.email | obfuscate | safe }}" property="email">{% registryIcon 'email' %}Email<span class="visually-hidden"> — {{ site.contact.email | spellEmail }}</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/AdrianoRutz/" rel="me sameAs noopener" target="_blank">{% registryIcon 'linkedin' %}LinkedIn</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/adafede" rel="me sameAs noopener" target="_blank">{% registryIcon 'github' %}GitHub</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="home__bio" about="wd:Q97455964">
    {{ curriculum.bio | renderMarkdown | safe }}
  </section>

  <section class="home__expertise" aria-labelledby="expertise-heading" about="wd:Q97455964">
    <h2 id="expertise-heading">Areas of expertise</h2>
    {% include "expertise.njk" %}
  </section>

</article>
